# Build output, and the corpora, seeds and crash artifacts a local run
# accumulates.
#
# `seeds/` is local-only on purpose. `./fuzz.sh seeds` generates a scratch set
# to warm up a laptop run, but nothing is committed: this substrate's decoder
# is total — every byte slice is a valid program — so libFuzzer bootstraps
# these targets from nothing, and committed seeds would only be 200 blobs that
# silently change meaning whenever a target's `Input` gains a field. Inputs
# genuinely worth keeping in git go in `regressions/<target>/`, which the cron
# replays before every campaign.
target
corpus
artifacts
coverage
seeds

# Tracked, overriding the repo-root rule: this workspace is not covered by the
# root lockfile, so without one here every CI run re-resolves from scratch and
# is at the mercy of upstream yanks.
!Cargo.lock
